Package: homelab-common
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         libmojo-pg-perl,
         libdbi-perl,
         libdbd-pg-perl,
         libminion-perl,
         postgresql-client
Breaks: homelab-database (<< 0.1.1), homelab-pgbouncer (<< 0.1.1)
Replaces: homelab-database (<< 0.1.1), homelab-pgbouncer (<< 0.1.1)
Description: Shared foundation library for every homelab-* feature package
 Config loading, database connections (both the narrow runtime role and
 the separate schema-migration role), a service-registry client, a
 Postgres-backed job-queue helper (Minion), a schema-migration runner,
 and a health-check-route helper. Every Mojolicious-based homelab-*
 feature depends on this instead of re-implementing the same plumbing —
 see the CLAUDE.md architecture notes in the source repository. Also
 ships homelab-bootstrap-app-role and homelab-bootstrap-pgbouncer-entry
 (the split-role DB/pgbouncer provisioning tools) here rather than in
 homelab-database/homelab-pgbouncer, so any feature can depend on the
 lightweight client tool without pulling in an entire local Postgres/
 pgbouncer server install.
